yamlover/anchor
description: An & path anchor before the value - this node also lives at that path
- >
  An **anchor** `&: P: k` before a value declares that the node ALSO lives at path P under key
  k - a REAL key, with no separate anchor namespace, so plain paths reach it. A trailing `[]`
  (`&P[]`) declares keyless appended MEMBERSHIP in a container; several anchors may stack. The
  deprecated `~key:` and `~-` back-edge spellings still parse through the migration window.
  YAML's `&name` maps to the document-scope `&: name` - the YAML anchor is the subclass:
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  boss: &: chief
    name: Rex
  team:
    lead: *: chief
- *..:..:..:..:..:..:04-yaml:01-yaml_code:00-yaml_structured:00-yaml_mapping:02-yaml_key_value_pair:01-yaml_anchor
